<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Islamic Courts Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2006">2006</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Islamic Courts Union was an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharia">sharia</a> courts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> that took control of Mogadishu in June 2006 after defeating US-backed warlords, bringing a brief period of order to the capital. Its expansion and the rise of hard-line factions provoked an Ethiopian invasion in December 2006 that drove it from power. Its militant youth wing, al-Shabaab, then launched a long insurgency.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/islamic-courts-union.jpg" alt="Islamic Courts Union" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guardafuuii · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ICU_Somalia_Emblem.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
